From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JP Hein <jp@jphein.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 2026 09:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH v9 1/2] media: uvcvideo: add UVC_QUIRK_CTRL_THROTTLE for
 fragile USB firmware

Some UVC devices have firmware that misbehaves under sustained rapid
USB control transfers. The Razer Kiyo Pro (1532:0e05) can lock up an
endpoint, which on some xHCI host controllers cascades to controller
death, taking every USB device on the bus down with it.

Add UVC_QUIRK_CTRL_THROTTLE, which enforces a uniform minimum interval
(100ms) between control transfers in __uvc_query_ctrl() -- the lowest-
level UVC control transfer function, so all callers are covered,
including uvc_set_video_ctrl() which bypasses uvc_query_ctrl().

This is a frequency-reducing mitigation, not a complete fix. usbmon
capture of real-world crashes shows the lockup can still occur on a
single stream reconfiguration (a SET_INTERFACE + COMMIT_CONTROL pair),
where there is no rapid transfer burst for a minimum-interval throttle
to pace. The host-controller cascade that follows is an xHCI-side
concern being addressed separately. Spacing out control traffic does
reduce how often the firmware is driven into the lockup, which is
worthwhile for an opt-in, device-table-gated quirk; non-quirked devices
are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: JP Hein <jp@jphein.com>
---
v8 -> v9: dropped the COMMIT-specific 200ms delay and the 10s COMMIT
  URB timeout from this quirk. usbmon analysis of real crashes showed
  the COMMIT hang is the second phase of a stream-reconfiguration lock,
  not a COMMIT-rate effect, and the extended timeout only lengthened the
  hang rather than aiding recovery. Reduced to the uniform interval and
  reframed as a frequency-reducing mitigation rather than a fix. See the
  cover letter and crash-evidence/2026-06-13-precursor-wire-captures/.

 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvcvideo.h  |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
index a5013a7..1d1206f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
@@ -36,6 +36,33 @@ static int __uvc_query_ctrl(struct uvc_device *dev, u8 query, u8 unit,
 	u8 type = USB_TYPE_CLASS | USB_RECIP_INTERFACE;
 	unsigned int pipe;

+	/*
+	 * Rate-limit control transfers for devices with fragile firmware.
+	 * The Razer Kiyo Pro locks up under sustained rapid control
+	 * transfers (hundreds without delay), which can cascade into xHCI
+	 * host-controller death. Throttle in this low-level function so all
+	 * callers are covered, including uvc_set_video_ctrl() which bypasses
+	 * uvc_query_ctrl().
+	 *
+	 * This is a frequency-reducing mitigation, not a guaranteed fix:
+	 * usbmon capture of real crashes shows the lockup can still occur on
+	 * a single stream reconfiguration (a SET_INTERFACE + COMMIT pair),
+	 * which no minimum-interval throttle can prevent. The resulting
+	 * host-controller cascade is an xHCI-side concern.
+	 */
+	if (dev->quirks & UVC_QUIRK_CTRL_THROTTLE) {
+		unsigned long min_interval = msecs_to_jiffies(100);
+
+		if (dev->last_ctrl_jiffies &&
+		    time_before(jiffies,
+				dev->last_ctrl_jiffies + min_interval)) {
+			unsigned long wait = dev->last_ctrl_jiffies +
+					     min_interval - jiffies;
+			msleep(jiffies_to_msecs(wait));
+		}
+		dev->last_ctrl_jiffies = jiffies;
+	}
+
 	pipe = (query & 0x80) ? usb_rcvctrlpipe(dev->udev, 0)
 			      : usb_sndctrlpipe(dev->udev, 0);
 	type |= (query & 0x80) ? USB_DIR_IN : USB_DIR_OUT;
diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvcvideo.h b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvcvideo.h
index 757254f..31f2af5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvcvideo.h
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvcvideo.h
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@
 #define UVC_QUIRK_INVALID_DEVICE_SOF	0x00010000
 #define UVC_QUIRK_MJPEG_NO_EOF		0x00020000
 #define UVC_QUIRK_MSXU_META		0x00040000
+#define UVC_QUIRK_CTRL_THROTTLE		0x00080000

 /* Format flags */
 #define UVC_FMT_FLAG_COMPRESSED		0x00000001
@@ -583,6 +584,8 @@ struct uvc_device {
 	struct usb_interface *intf;
 	unsigned long warnings;
 	u32 quirks;
+	/* UVC control transfer throttling (UVC_QUIRK_CTRL_THROTTLE) */
+	unsigned long last_ctrl_jiffies;
 	int intfnum;
 	char name[32];

--
2.43.0
